<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Koloniale Staten</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1866">1866</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Colonial States of Suriname</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Koloniale Staten was the colonial legislature of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a>, established in 1866. Most of its members were elected by a small electorate qualified by income and education, the rest appointed by the governor, so that it represented a narrow wealthy class. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/universal-suffrage">Universal suffrage</a> was introduced in 1948, and the body became the parliament of autonomous Suriname, the forerunner of today's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-assembly-of-france">National Assembly</a>.</p></div>
